{"parentUuid":"ad19da58-6230-4bf3-814f-9e5b5f7f47eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFYY6YVeSgaHzX1LLL47","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added two more graphics improvements on `hedgerow-grass`; nothing is pushed. Together with the flares (0f66dad5), they aren't in `hedgerow-poc` yet, and a trial merge onto its newest commit (d65f16e9) has no conflicts. All six tests pass, and the costs below were measured in a headless browser on the M1 Max.\n\n- **Flare light in shafts, and tree crowns that cast shadows (09e7b09c):**\n  - While a flare burns, its light hangs in the rain over the street, and the roofs and chimneys cut dark beams into it.\n  - The tree crowns now cast shadows under the flare too, not just the trunks, so the forest floor is dappled.\n  - My first strength washed the street out in an even haze, so it's now at 40% of that.\n  - Both together cost under 0.3 ms a frame in the forest. Nothing runs when no flare is burning.\n- **Temporal anti-aliasing (2c09b946):** under lamps and flares, each wet cobble's highlight was a harsh single-pixel sparkle, and grass and twigs shimmered as you moved. Now the cobbles read as a smooth sheen.\n  - A fast pan and a walking soldier showed no trails behind objects.\n  - Rain, sparks, tracers and muzzle flashes would have faded almost to nothing through it, so they're now drawn after it and stay crisp.\n  - It costs about 0.3 ms and is on for high and medium; low is unchanged.\n\nTwo things matter for your first-person work, and both are in the shared notes file:\n- **The rifle and hands:** TAA treats anything nearer than 1.2 m as moving with the camera.\n- **Camera jumps:** a jump of more than 2 m in one frame restarts its history, which covers teleports and the death camera.\n\nThe jitter wraps the render call in `main.js`; I didn't touch `camera.js`.\n\nI tried raindrops beaded on the rifle and sleeves but dropped them: at this resolution they read as noise.\n\nTesting used a headless Chrome on the real GPU, so nothing appeared in your browser pane; starting it needed the sandbox turned off for that one command. It and the server are stopped, and I removed `launch.json`, which held only my entry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":250,"cache_read_input_tokens":827375,"output_tokens":747,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":250,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":827375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":250},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"af7c76d4-c1ba-4425-a0ed-de5c4e9f1bad","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFYY5qqCoqsQ5TtLeP87","requestRef":"82fbcdef-ca3a-43da-9c83-cd649649f8d5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"7409093b-83e1-42d1-a484-a4687da29858","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:31:53.233Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
