{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"282e237902336592a78c0c7fa6657250850ceea4c068dcc5edc0fa2ed6b21934","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The haze has no measurable performance cost—both runs hold the 120 fps cap, with the effect subtly visible on the truck's hoops and flames. I'm now fixing a bug where blasts behind the camera flip the push direction by skipping shells whose centre falls behind the view.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B62ftCHBTbUAGz7Bi417bi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/distort.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"      vec4 c = uViewProj * vec4(s.xyz, 1.0);\n      vec2 cuv = c.xy / c.w * 0.5 + 0.5;\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"      vec4 c = uViewProj * vec4(s.xyz, 1.0);\n      if (c.w <= 0.0) continue;        // a blast behind the camera: no ring to see\n      vec2 cuv = c.xy / c.w * 0.5 + 0.5;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\nnode --check js/distort.js && L=\"$TMPDIR\"; for t in world-check lod-check distance-check ai-check fp-check clutter-check; do [ -f tests/$t.mjs ] || continue; node tests/$t.mjs > \"$L/$t.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"$t ok\" || { echo \"$t FAILED\"; tail -5 \"$L/$t.log\"; }; done; grep -n \"after it so they stay crisp · \\`dof.js\\`\" README.md","description":"Skip shockwaves behind the camera and run the tests","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
