{"parentUuid":"b2544171-85de-4692-87c8-0ce028a773a3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFZWePy6qFTAfhY3jEZQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added heat haze over fires and shockwaves from explosions, committed on `hedgerow-grass` as d57e5389; nothing is pushed. Four of my commits are now waiting to go into `hedgerow-poc`: the flares, the light shafts, TAA and this one. A trial merge onto its newest commit (d65f16e9) has no conflicts, and all six tests pass.\n\n- **Heat haze:** hot air shimmers in a column above each of the four nearest fires, such as the burning truck in the street. It's subtle against the fog, as real heat shimmer is, and shows most on the truck's frame and flames.\n- **Shockwaves:** a grenade or charge sends out a ring that pushes the picture outwards as it races past, for half a second. At 12 m it bent about 65,000 pixels, a clear wave. Nothing shows for a blast behind you.\n- Walls in front of a fire aren't bent, and neither is the rifle in your hands.\n- It costs too little to measure: the frame rate stayed at the 120 fps cap with it on or off.\n\nWhile checking this, I found faint pre-existing rounding noise. Adding any extra full-screen pass to the effects chain, even a plain copy, changes about 150 pixels by 3–7 levels along a thin diagonal line. Neither version shows a visible seam, so I left it and wrote it up in the shared notes file. It isn't caused by the new pass.\n\nTesting used the headless browser again, which needed the sandbox turned off to start. It and the server are stopped, and `launch.json` is removed. It held only my entry, and the file hadn't existed before this round."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":793547,"output_tokens":532,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":793547,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"eefa1ebc-05e4-4494-b8b6-c6d90d13ac41","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFZWdrUiCKVZFdTr2BWK","requestRef":"5d57850d-a420-4844-9cc9-67cb82ec9be1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"e256a84a-f6f0-4643-9bb3-06786c3a2458","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:44:38.192Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
