{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"bd219fa72c5c5b60d8c22107f4d5d79593b8da865e8e2744140b2ea47c811a9d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll add a `lightning()` hook to `flares.js` that drives a blue-white shadowed directional light along a randomized strike direction (14–31° elevation) in short pulsed bursts, and dial back the ambient boost in `lights.js` so the shadows and light shafts read clearly.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hmke6V8HcpWh3zqJzzyL4a","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'js/flares.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nrep = [\n(\"\"\"   rain; the cloud deck round it lights up (sky.js) and it trails smoke\n   (effects.js). Nothing about it touches the fighting: the enemy sees as\n   well as before. */\"\"\",\n \"\"\"   rain; the cloud deck round it lights up (sky.js) and it trails smoke\n   (effects.js). Nothing about it touches the fighting: the enemy sees as\n   well as before.\n\n   When no flare burns, a lightning stroke (weather.js) takes the same\n   light for its fraction of a second: blue-white from the bolt's direction,\n   low over the horizon, so houses, walls, soldiers and trees throw long hard\n   shadows and its light stands in the rain in shafts (lightning()). */\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  const toFlare = new THREE.Vector3();\n  let frame = 0;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"  const toFlare = new THREE.Vector3();\n  let frame = 0;\n  const FLARE_COL = new THREE.Color('#eef4ff'), BOLT_COL = new THREE.Color('#d6e2ff');\n  const boltDir = new THREE.Vector3();\n  let struck = false, boltFrame = 0;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    if (!f.popped) {\n      f.popped = true;\n      f.vx = wind.x * 0.9; f.vz = wind.z * 0.9; f.vy = -2.4;\"\"\",\n \"\"\"    if (!f.popped) {\n      f.popped = true;\n      struck = false;\n      sun.color.copy(FLARE_COL);\n      f.vx = wind.x * 0.9; f.vz = wind.z * 0.9; f.vy = -2.4;\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  return {\n    update, light: sun, castersOf,\"\"\",\n \"\"\"  /* this frame's lightning (weather.js: its flash, the direction of the strike): when no\n     flare burns, the stroke lights the scene through the same light, with its shadows */\n  function lightning(flash, dir, cam) {\n    if (f && f.popped) return;                 // a burning flare holds the light\n    if (flash <= 0.02) {\n      if (struck) { struck = false; sun.intensity = 0; }\n      return;\n    }\n    // a new strike (another direction): its shadows drawn again from the start\n    if (!struck || boltDir.distanceToSquared(dir) > 1e-6) { boltDir.copy(dir); boltFrame = 0; }\n    struck = true;\n    sun.color.copy(BOLT_COL);\n    sun.intensity = 6 * flash;\n    const gy = G.terrain.height(cam.x, cam.z);\n    sun.target.position.set(cam.x, gy, cam.z);\n    sun.position.copy(boltDir).multiplyScalar(220).add(sun.target.position);\n    sun.target.updateMatrixWorld();\n    if (sun.castShadow && (boltFrame++ & 1) === 0) sun.shadow.needsUpdate = true;\n  }\n\n  return {\n    update, lightning, light: sun, castersOf,\"\"\"),\n]\nfor a, b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:60]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\n\np = 'js/lights.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    hemi.intensity = 3.2 + lightning * 3.0;\n    key.intensity = 1.2 + lightning * 2.5;\n    key.position.set(cam.x + 60, 25 + lightning * 40, cam.z + 30);\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    // lightning lifts the sky's light a little; its hard light comes from the bolt (flares.js)\n    hemi.intensity = 3.2 + lightning * 1.4;\n    key.intensity = 1.2 + lightning * 0.6;\n    key.position.set(cam.x + 60, 25 + lightning * 40, cam.z + 30);\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\n\np = 'js/main.js'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"    G.flares.update(dt, camera.position, { x: 1.4, z: 0.6 }, G.sky);\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    G.flares.update(dt, camera.position, { x: 1.4, z: 0.6 }, G.sky);\n    G.flares.lightning(flash, G.weather.flashDir, camera.position);\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\nfor f in js/flares.js js/lights.js js/main.js; do node --check $f || echo FAIL $f; done; grep -n \"const flash = G.weather.update\" js/main.js","description":"Let lightning drive the shadowed sky light"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
