{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"16d04702f960e6ea225dcb7a32e8f98cc95df0e0a45d471f8eb67f8b1ef37efb","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P4t1tMFkNiTa5kdK7ZHuSo","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    column of earth and roll dust along the ground), `atmosphere.js`\n    (halos, mist, decals),","new_string":"    column of earth and roll dust along the ground), `flames.js` (the\n    fires as flame: three billboards per near fire, each a turbulent body\n    of flame worked out in its shader, licking up in tongues, coloured by\n    its heat from deep red to a yellow-white core), `atmosphere.js`\n    (halos, mist, decals),"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MdisK5DLsBi9Fd7SPAx6V5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/flames.js fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: fires burn as flame\n\nThe fires (the burning truck in the street, the house, the flak gun once\nblown) were sprays of flame sprites from a point: a few orange blobs in\nthe truck's cab windows. Now each fire within 60 m carries three upright\nbillboards turned to the camera (flames.js), each a body of flame worked\nout in its shader: noise rising through a shape wide at a ragged base and\nlicking up to points, broken into tongues and eaten away from the top,\ncoloured by its heat like a black body - deep red at the edges, mostly\norange, yellow, white only at the hottest - bright enough to bloom. It is\ndrawn with the late particles after the anti-aliasing (the flicker stays\ncrisp), hidden behind what stands in front and soft where it meets the\ncab or the wall; without the effects chain it is drawn with the scene.\nThe sprite flames thin to a third, licks over the body; the smoke and\nembers stay. Too cheap to measure at 1024x768 on an M1 Max.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Commit the shader flames and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
