{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"c98dffa9a1aa51f26f753842b9fa550a504aef2ab976eec4a68eb40e05ce10d4","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AdQEuA9DgKLFDdyWYwNyvT","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"lamps and the glow of the sky, broken by rain rings, river banks soaked\nabove the waterline, a forest floor","new_string":"lamps and the glow of the sky, broken by rain rings, river banks soaked\nabove the waterline with a thin broken line of scum where the water laps\nthem and the water browner in the shallows of the ford, a forest floor"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013573tWgBRD57Xid5PgE6wp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the river laps its banks; shallows at the ford\n\nThe river was one dark glossy sheet that met its banks in a hard line.\nIts shader now knows its own depth (the ground map's mesh-exact height,\nread through the grass map the terrain already shares): where it laps\nthe bank a thin, broken line of scum drifts with the current, its reach\nbreathing a little, matte and reflecting nothing (the reflections pass\nskips it); in the shallows (under 0.75 m: the ford, the edges) it turns\nbrowner, the bed showing through. Streaks of foam down the middle were\ntried and dropped: thresholded value noise read as rows of white dashes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Commit the river shore and shallows"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
