{"parentUuid":"e7476ef9-c567-479b-b5d2-593d6bf0d427","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFaQR9hY9in36fJbe5kQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I committed three more graphics improvements on `hedgerow-grass`; nothing is pushed. With the earlier ones, seven commits are waiting to go into `hedgerow-poc` (from 0f66dad5 to df6bc348). A trial merge onto its newest commit (d65f16e9) has no conflicts, and all six tests pass.\n\n- **Lightning throws hard shadows (3d5edb83):** a lightning stroke used to just brighten everything evenly. Now, when no flare is burning, it uses the flare's shadow-casting light, aimed from the bolt and low over the horizon.\n  - For each flash the village is lit cold blue-white, and a building's shadow cuts straight across the street.\n  - The light also hangs in the rain in shafts, and under the canopy the floor shows shafts of light between tree shadows.\n  - The shadow work only runs during strokes, under a second each.\n- **Fires burn as flame (218c39a5):** the burning truck was a few orange blobs in its cab windows. Now each nearby fire has animated flames drawn by a shader, rising from a ragged base in separate tongues.\n  - They're mostly orange, with deep red at the edges and white only at the hottest point.\n  - From down the street the truck and the house both read clearly as burning, at no measurable cost.\n- **The river laps its banks (df6bc348):** a thin, broken line of scum drifts along the water's edge, and the water turns brown in the shallows of the ford, where you can see the bed.\n  - My first attempt had current streaks that looked like road-marking dashes, plus a glaring white shoreline. I removed the streaks and thinned the shoreline.\n\nThe shared notes file lists every file each commit touches, for whoever merges. Testing ran in the headless browser again, which needed the sandbox off to start. It and the server are stopped, and I removed `launch.json`, which held only my entry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_read_input_tokens":875684,"output_tokens":622,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":622,"cache_read_input_tokens":875684,"cache_creation_input_tokens":235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"17350268-ff5d-41bf-935c-382113de8edc","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFaQQYUwzcsXNvMPwo1r","requestRef":"f59be93e-0111-4f34-8adf-e5abe3ce7ddc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"adefb389-200c-4f99-9c95-41936350b80c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:56:21.958Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
