{"parentUuid":"5cadaae9-f811-4e60-b04a-cb9ec26117eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFahXuiHgZz2eyZWMoiv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NPemM9bBHz4JTpuUpfzC8b","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np = 'README.md'\ns = open(p).read()\nold = \"\"\"  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials (and close-up bark on the\n    baked trunks: the bark detail projected in the tree's own space from\n    two sides, per species) · `sky.js`, `weather.js`\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"  * `materials.js` palette-keyed wet materials (and close-up bark on the\n    baked trunks: the bark detail projected in the tree's own space from\n    two sides, per species; rain running down walls within ~24 m in\n    rivulets that slide down and catch the light) · `sky.js`, `weather.js`\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd ../.. && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain runs down the walls\n\nWet walls were only darker. Now, within ~24 m, water runs down every\nvertical face of the world in rivulets (materials.js, the weather shader's\nstreaks): columns ~22 cm apart, each wandering as it runs, carrying water\nin stretches that slide down at about a metre a second; a rivulet is a\ndarker wet stripe with a glossy core, and bulges out of the wall enough to\ncatch a lamp's or a flare's light across it. Scaled by the rain. Not on\nthe soldiers, their kit or their weapons (by name and palette key, and\nnothing skinned).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2 && (git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"merges cleanly into hedgerow-poc\" || echo \"merge conflicts\")","description":"Commit the rivulets and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"co