{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","id":"ec7b122a-e9cb-4b96-82b8-0f38339eaa99","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:05:53.128Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"aca1d33e67df77c08846866245a8b157faabfdb8617ed3a1eb9cac3e5556c296","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"2aa544e2-fe28-43e5-bcaa-77f6e2e857bf","keep":1466,"tail":["d3b89f284f2f0dd69d73f4499770f4c2ad710cc5b47e1c0b448125278fdded7b","701df532231cc90e862ae4e1224302075915753c5f20eec238ade39b4d95ffac","a6ad48231c8dfd357e4e273e2a73201aac4e89ee87824a380dc26100e8f7a937"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1468,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"18321b753d423f1aa84815a17cdf28c5008b2937cc8c6d9e6766d838918b722b"}
{"parentUuid":"890d92be-a56a-40e2-9e38-af72fde66fa8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFb957PG9pdxfDq8UQUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added two graphics improvements and one important fix, all committed on `hedgerow-grass`; nothing is pushed. Ten commits are now waiting to go into `hedgerow-poc` (0f66dad5 to 2839fe62). A trial merge onto its newest commit (d65f16e9) has no conflicts, and all six tests pass.\n\n- **Rain runs down the walls (e0615fa2):** within about 24 m, water runs down every wall in darker wet stripes with a glossy core, sliding down at about a metre a second. It's subtle, and best seen under lamps and in motion. Soldiers, their kit and weapons don't get it.\n- **Fix: depth through the effects (a0b204b2):** while adding motion blur I found a bug from my TAA round.\n  - TAA writes into the scene's buffer, and three.js clears that buffer's depth before drawing. Every effect after it was reading an empty depth.\n  - As a result, flames and particles weren't hidden behind walls: the truck's flames showed through its cab.\n  - The heat haze ignored walls, and aiming lost its depth of field entirely.\n  - The scene depth is now preserved through the whole effects chain. I confirmed real distances come back (rifle at 0.83 m, hands at 0.3–0.5 m) and that aiming focuses again.\n  - Your branch never had this bug, since TAA isn't on it yet. When merging, take this fix together with the TAA commit (2c09b946), never TAA alone. That's at the top of the shared notes file.\n- **Camera motion blur (2839fe62):** turning or moving now smears the street along the motion, while the rifle and hands stay sharp, and so do the rain and sparks. It's skipped when the view is still or jumps, and is on for high and medium.\n\nA side effect of the fix: the truck's flames are now correctly hidden by the cab and glow through its windows. My earlier flame captures had been drawn through the cab because of the bug, so you'll see less of them.\n\nTesting used the headless browser again, which needed the sandbox off to start. It and the server are stopped, and I removed `launch.json`, which held only my entry."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_read_input_tokens":940761,"output_tokens":707,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":940761,"cache_creation_input_tokens":243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":243},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2d803cc5-1598-4d29-bc46-155ca0aed108","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgFb94PyStCb8RcxNWqm8","requestRef":"ec7b122a-e9cb-4b96-82b8-0f38339eaa99","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc97f2aa-8fd0-4221-9087-8aac53311f70","timestamp":"2026-10-21T15:06:01.171Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-poc","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
